<title>SWEDEN: H&amp;M H1 profit rises 63 pct to 1.01 bln Skr.</title>
<headline>H&amp;M H1 profit rises 63 pct to 1.01 bln Skr.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months from December 1, 1996 to May 31, 1997,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    1,006 vs   618</p>
<p> Turnover including VAT		 10,179 vs 7,771</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	    3.16 vs  1.94</p>
<p> Operating costs			  7,452  vs 5,807</p>
<p> Depreciation				 146  vs   120</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	1,013  vs   646</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE   40  vs    42 CHARGE</p>
<p> Set-up costs				  47  vs    70</p>
<p> Tax					    352  vs   216</p>
<p>NOTE -- Swedish fashion retailer H&amp;M Hennes &amp; Mauritz AB was expected to post a 35 percent lift in profits after financial items of 832 million crowns for the first six months of 1996/97, a Reuters poll showed.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
